                        75.0
                    ],
                    "text": "click-free gain in dB: -72 = silent, 0 = unchanged, up to +35. The gain glides along a 10 ms smoother, so a jump never clicks, and the bottom lands on true silence. The gain inlet takes a number or a signal (an LFO). State outlet (last): every number that changes the gain goes out as gain <dB> (e.g. gain -6.), through [change 0.] so repeats are dropped. Signals feed the gen~ only and are not reported.",
                    "fontname": "Arial",
                    "fontsize": 12.0
